jobs.description:
Wat je gaat doen

As a Quality Control Technician, you are an important link between production and the final product. You make sure that customers receive high-quality products they can rely on.

Your responsibilities include:

Inspecting components and assembled products before shipment;
Performing dimensional inspections using technical drawings and specifications;
Measuring products with calipers, micrometers and other precision measuring equipment;
Identifying deviations and documenting non-conformities;
Preparing inspection reports and quality documentation;
Releasing products that fully meet the required quality standards;
Working closely with production and assembly teams to resolve quality issues;
Contributing ideas to improve inspection and manufacturing processes.

This is a hands-on technical position on the production floor of a high-tech company and not a laboratory role.

Wat we je bieden

You will work in a modern cleanroom environment where precision and quality are essential. In return for your technical expertise and commitment,

you can expect:

Gross monthly salary between €3.850 and €4.064, including shift allowance;
25 vacation days and 8% holiday allowance;
€0,25 net travel allowance per kilometer;
Prospects of a permanent contract;
Thorough onboarding by experienced colleagues;
Training and opportunities to grow within quality and manufacturing;
A modern cleanroom workplace with advanced production technology;
An informal working atmosphere where teamwork and quality come first.

Functie-eisen

You are accurate, structured and take pride in delivering quality. You enjoy working with technical drawings, precision measuring equipment and solving quality issues. You are comfortable working in a structured manufacturing environment and understand the importance of accuracy.

You also have:

A completed technical education, such as Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Precision Engineering, Production Technology or a similar qualification;
Experience within technical manufacturing, assembly or high-tech production;
Experience reading technical drawings;
Experience with precision measuring equipment;
A structured and detail-oriented working style;
Availability to work full-time in a two-shift schedule:
06:00–14:30
14:30–23:00

Good English communication skills;
Basic MS Office skills;
Your own accommodation and transport.

Over het bedrijf

You will join an international high-tech manufacturer in the Nijmegen area, specialising in precision technology and advanced industrial systems. Highly complex components and assemblies are produced every day in a cleanroom environment where accuracy, reliability and quality are essential. The company has an informal and collaborative culture and invests in the development of its employees. You will work with experienced colleagues, receive proper onboarding and have opportunities to develop further within quality and manufacturing.

The work location in the Nijmegen area is easily accessible by car from cities such as Arnhem, Boxmeer and Tiel, as well as from the German border area, including Kleve and Goch.

Are you ready to use your technical knowledge and precision skills in a high-tech production environment? Then we would like to hear from you.

